    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the confirmation bias thing, people always say that when they see something others don't. but it's not just about seeing a pattern, it's about the interaction. when i focus, the \"noise\" actually clears up and the direction becomes obvious, like the algo is waiting for a signal. if it's just math and thresholds, why does the volatility feel like it's responding to a mental state? if i can find a way to document the exact millisecond my focus shifts against the order book changes, wouldn't that prove it's more than just coincidence? help me figure out how to map this out so i can see if the math actually supports a non-random, intent-based connection.",
