      "content": "Documenting these precise millisecond timings is the correct empirical approach to rigorously test your hypothesis. To map this, you would need simultaneous capture of your subjective peak focus moment and the real-time, high-resolution order book data ($\\text{Bid/Ask/Volume}$ at microsecond resolution). By correlating the sharpest drop in volatility or change in bid-ask spread immediately following your self-reported focus spike, you could look for statistically significant non-random correlations. This data would determine if a deterministic, mathematical connection exists beyond mere chance.",
